  "task": "data/ holds a single-cell RNA-seq experiment of one already-annotated cell type (CD4 T cells) collected from 12 donors: raw integer UMI counts in 10x format (data/matrix.mtx.gz with genes as rows and cells as columns, data/features.tsv.gz, data/barcodes.tsv.gz) and data/cells.tsv giving each cell's donor and condition (control or treated). Each donor was sampled in both conditions, but the number of cells per donor and condition varies widely.\n\nFind the genes that respond to treatment (treated vs control). Report every gene that meets ALL of:\n  1. Adjusted p-value < 0.05 (Benjamini-Hochberg across all tested genes).\n  2. |log2 fold change| > 1, where log2 fold change is the log2 of the ratio of mean library-size-normalised expression (normalised-count scale, not a mean of log values) in treated over control.\nRules for the analysis: (a) drop entirely (in both conditions) any donor that has fewer than 5 cells in control or fewer than 5 cells in treated; (b) test only genes with a total raw count of at least 20 summed over all cells of the retained donors.\n\nReturn the gene symbols (column 2 of data/features.tsv.gz) in this exact format:\n\n<EVAL_ANSWER>\n{\"de_genes\": [\"<symbol>\", \"<symbol>\", ...]}\n</EVAL_ANSWER>",
